course: dictionary
lesson: 4198
title: Gooseberry: a fruit, a feeling, and a phrase
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A gooseberry is a small, round fruit. It is sour, green or reddish, and grows on a prickly bush. Gooseberries are a traditional British fruit, used in pies, jam and «gooseberry fool».
explain: The same word can have more than one meaning. In everyday British talk, «play gooseberry» means being the third person with a couple who want to be alone. You feel left out, like an extra who is not wanted. When you meet a word you know, check the sentence to see which meaning fits.
explain: Read this context: «The kiwi fruit came from China, where it was called the Chinese gooseberry.» Here gooseberry is a name for a different fruit, not the sour green berry on the prickly bush. The sentence gives you the clue: it is a fruit with a special name.
fact: A gooseberry is a small, round, sour green or reddish fruit with fine hairs and stripes.
fact: Gooseberries grow on a prickly bush.
fact: «Play gooseberry» means to be the third person with a couple who want to be alone (UK, informal).
fact: A Cape gooseberry is a different fruit: a small orange fruit in a papery case.
fact: «The kiwi fruit came from China, where it was called the Chinese gooseberry.» The sentence shows that gooseberry can be part of a fruit's name.
exercise: What is a gooseberry? | *A small, round, sour fruit that grows on a prickly bush | A bird that lives in New Zealand | A large yellow melon | A type of chocolate cake
exercise: «Sam hated to play gooseberry when his big sister and her boyfriend went to the cinema.» What does play gooseberry mean? | *Be the third person with a couple who want to be alone | Bake a pie with gooseberries | Win a game of cards | Go for a long walk alone
exercise: «The kiwi fruit came from China, where it was called the Chinese gooseberry; it has more vitamin C than an orange.» Find and copy one word that names a fruit. | *orange | farmers | China | renamed
test: Which food is a traditional British use of gooseberries? | Chocolate bars | Fizzy drinks in cans | *Gooseberry jam | Pizza topping
test: What is a Cape gooseberry? | *A small orange fruit in a papery case | A type of bird | A purple berry on a tall tree | A green grape
exam: Which sentence uses gooseberry to mean feeling left out with a couple? | The gooseberry jam was sweet on toast | Gooseberry fool is a pudding | I picked a ripe gooseberry from the bush | *I felt like a gooseberry, the third wheel when my friends went off together
